│ R7 EVIDENCE · 4/9 · < Cycle | Hunts / probes >
│   R7 EVIDENCE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── observed, not a guarantee
│
│   All loaded cores share one voltage rail, set by the loaded core with the highest voltage request. R7 attribution keeps a separate top-request group on each
│   loaded CCD: the cores within 1 mV of that CCD's highest request, tied. An unattributed failure is charged to the affected CCD's top group first, and that
│   group need not contain the core that sets the rail.
│   Request order is read from the telemetry recorded for each CCD's full part. `per offset order` marks a CCD where no measurement covers a loaded core, so
│   the order is taken from the offsets instead.
│   Self-sufficient means the core has been observed passing as a top requester at its current offset or deeper. That is evidence so far, not a guarantee
│   against future failures.
│
│   While this R7 trial runs, any outcome is conditional: its end may add request or clock telemetry that changes the top requesters, the backoff targets and
│   the partials derived from them.
